WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.874
Automaticity is practiced execution with reduced conscious effort.

00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:07.924
It allows routine components of a task to run smoothly so the performer can reserve

00:00:07.924 --> 00:00:08.839
attention for judgment,

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:10.207
monitoring, and adaptation.

00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:12.868
A skilled operator, engineer, analyst, writer,

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:16.918
or communicator may perform common steps fluently because those steps have been practiced

00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:18.082
many times with feedback.

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.687
Automaticity is powerful because attention is limited.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.802
Working memory can only hold and process a small amount at once.

00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:26.016
If every basic step consumes full attention,

00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:28.626
there is little capacity left for higher-level decisions.

00:00:28.626 --> 00:00:32.061
When routine components become efficient, the performer can notice exceptions,

00:00:32.061 --> 00:00:34.835
coordinate with others, and think about the larger situation.

00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:35.955
The risk is autopilot.

00:00:35.955 --> 00:00:39.235
Fluent behavior can continue even when the situation has changed.

00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:43.224
In high-risk work, experts still need checklists, procedures, deliberate pauses,

00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:46.734
and peer review because memory and attention can fail under pressure, fatigue,

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:47.658
or interruption.

00:00:47.658 --> 00:00:49.553
These supports do not replace expertise.

00:00:49.553 --> 00:00:52.278
They protect expertise from predictable human limits.

00:00:52.278 --> 00:00:55.432
Attention control includes focus routines and interruption management.

00:00:55.432 --> 00:00:59.862
Before important work, a performer may clarify the goal, remove avoidable distractions,

00:00:59.862 --> 00:01:02.916
set up required tools, and define when to pause or escalate.

00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:05.046
During the work, they may use checkbacks, notes,

00:01:05.046 --> 00:01:07.311
or short reviews to keep track of assumptions.

00:01:07.311 --> 00:01:12.230
The point is to make attention a managed resource rather than hoping it will remain stable

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:12.240
by itself.
